{"name":"Trail Dust","hex":"#d0c4ac","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To follow behind (someone or something); to tail (someone or something).","To drag (something) behind on the ground."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The track or indication marking the route followed by something that has passed, such as the footprints of animal on land or the contrail of an airplane in the sky.","A route for travel over land, especially a narrow, unpaved pathway for use by hikers, horseback riders, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail"},{"term":"dust","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Fine particles.\n Fine, dry particles of matter found in the air and covering the surface of objects, typically consisting of soil lifted up by the wind, pollen, hair, fiber debris, dead skin cells, etc.\n\n Any substance reduced to fine particles; powder.\n Submicron particles in outer space, largely silicates and carbon compounds, that contribute greatly to extinction at visible wavelengths.\n\n Disintegration of a solid, like silica.\n Flour.\n A single fine, dry particle of earth or other material; grain of dust.","Fine, dry particles of matter found in the air and covering the surface of objects, typically consisting of soil lifted up by the wind, pollen, hair, fiber debris, dead skin cells, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove dust from.","To remove dust; to clean by removing dust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trail Dust","blocks":[{"text":"Trail Dust is a 1936 American Western film directed by Nate Watt, written by Al Martin, and starring William Boyd, James Ellison, George \"Gabby\" Hayes, Morris Ankrum, Gwynne Shipman, Britt Wood and Dick Dickson. It was released on December 11, 1936, by Paramount Pictures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f0/Trail_Dust_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trail_Dust","wikidata":"Q3818214"},{"title":"Trail Dust (1924 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Trail Dust is a 1924 American silent Western film directed by Gordon Hines and starring David Dunbar, Louise McComb and William Lenders. Portraying settlers in nineteenth century Oklahoma Territory, it was shot on location at the 101 Ranch in the state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Trail_Dust_%281924%29_-_1.jpg/330px-Trail_Dust_%281924%29_-_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trail_Dust_(1924_film)","wikidata":"Q65071187"},{"title":"Trail","blocks":[{"text":"A trail, also known as a path or track, is a dirt road or a small paved road, usually through an undeveloped natural area, that is designed primarily for use by pedestrians, equestrians and non-motorized vehicles, although occasionally some off-roading motor vehicles may also use it. In the United Kingdom and Ireland, footpath or hiking trail is the preferred term. However, it is sometimes applied to highways in North America. In the United States, the term was historically used to describe the westward expansion trails, which are land routes into or through wildness regions of the American West used by explorers and migrants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Trail_between_two_fields_%28Slovenia%2C_Selo_pri_Mirni%29.jpg/330px-Trail_between_two_fields_%28Slovenia%2C_Selo_pri_Mirni%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trail","wikidata":"Q628179"},{"title":"Dust","blocks":[{"text":"Dust is made of fine particles of solid matter. On Earth, it generally consists of particles in the atmosphere that come from various sources such as soil lifted by wind, volcanic eruptions, and pollution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Dust_storm_approaching_Stratford%2C_Texas.jpg/330px-Dust_storm_approaching_Stratford%2C_Texas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dust","wikidata":"Q165632"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/MountainBikeTrail.jpg/500px-MountainBikeTrail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/MountainBikeTrail.jpg/1280px-MountainBikeTrail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/MountainBikeTrail.jpg/500px-MountainBikeTrail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mountain bike trail in the Forest of Dean, England","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMountainBikeTrail.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Kruununpuisto_Imatra.JPG/500px-Kruununpuisto_Imatra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Kruununpuisto_Imatra.JPG/1280px-Kruununpuisto_Imatra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Kruununpuisto_Imatra.JPG/500px-Kruununpuisto_Imatra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Trail in the Kruununpuisto Nature Park in Imatra, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKruununpuisto_Imatra.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Rain_Forest_in_KLIA.jpg/500px-Rain_Forest_in_KLIA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Rain_Forest_in_KLIA.jpg/1280px-Rain_Forest_in_KLIA.jpg?utm_source=en.